        "Alexei Kitaev",
        "Andrew M. Steane",
        "Peter W. Shor"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Quantum error correction and fault tolerance established that scalable quantum computation is physically possible despite decoherence, a foundational advance with broad experimental consequence.",
        "attribution": "Shor supplied the decisive error-correction and computational breakthrough; Steane and Kitaev made distinct, enduring contributions to practical and topological code architectures.",
        "maturity": "The principles have been tested extensively across hardware platforms and now organize the central experimental challenge of quantum computing.",
        "uncertainties": [
