      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory gave strongly correlated electrons a broadly useful nonperturbative theoretical framework and reshaped computational condensed-matter physics.",
        "attribution": "Georges, Kotliar, and Vollhardt made defining contributions to the formulation and establishment of the method.",
        "maturity": "It is a durable standard tool whose predictions and extensions are deeply embedded in correlated-materials research.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "A prize citation must clearly delimit the original theoretical advance from the large subsequent methodological ecosystem."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 8,
      "ballot_id": "B012",
